<section class="wrap prose">
  <h2>The capitals that catch everyone out</h2>
  <p>The usual traps are countries whose largest or best-known city is not the capital: Australia (Canberra, not Sydney), Canada (Ottawa, not Toronto), Turkey (Ankara, not Istanbul), Brazil (Brasília, not Rio de Janeiro or São Paulo), Nigeria (Abuja, not Lagos) and Myanmar (Naypyidaw, not Yangon). A few countries list more than one capital — South Africa splits government between Pretoria, Cape Town and Bloemfontein, and Bolivia between Sucre and La Paz; the quiz uses the first listed in our dataset.</p>
  <p>Every capital in this quiz links to a full country profile in the <a href="../atlas/index.html">atlas</a>.</p>
</section>
